<article class="env-lemma" id="0B2J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B2J">Lemma <span data-tag="0B2J">33.19.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ be a morphism from an irreducible scheme to the spectrum of a valuation ring. If $f$ is locally of finite type and surjective, then the special fibre is equidimensional of dimension equal to the dimension of the generic fibre. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may replace $X$ by its reduction because this does not change the dimension of $X$ or of the special fibre. Then $X$ is integral and the lemma follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00QK" data-tag="00QK">10.125.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>